      "slug": "the-tribute-money-masaccio",
      "title": "The Tribute Money (Masaccio)",
      "year": 1424,
      "imageUrl": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b3/The_Tribute_Money_by_Masaccio.jpg",
      "imageWidth": 2200,
      "imageHeight": 1015,
      "story": "The Tribute Money is a fresco by the Italian Early Renaissance painter Masaccio, located in the Brancacci Chapel of the basilica of Santa Maria del Carmine, Florence. Painted in the 1420s, it is widely considered among Masaccio's best work, and a vital part of the development of Renaissance art.",
      "facts": [
        "The chapel passed to Pietro's nephew, Felice Brancacci, who some time between 1423 and 1425 commissioned the painter Masolino to decorate the walls with a series of frescoes from the life of Saint Peter.",
        "Over the centuries the frescoes were greatly altered and damaged.",
        "It was not until the years 1981–1990 that a full-scale restoration of the chapel was undertaken, restoring the frescoes to approximately their original state."
      ],
