      "title": "Expulsion from the Garden of Eden",
      "year": 1424,
      "imageUrl": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/37/Masaccio-TheExpulsionOfAdamAndEveFromEden-Restoration.jpg",
      "imageWidth": 913,
      "imageHeight": 1173,
      "story": "The Expulsion from the Garden of Eden is a fresco by the Italian Early Renaissance artist Masaccio. The fresco is a single scene from the cycle painted around 1425 by Masaccio, Masolino and others on the walls of the Brancacci Chapel in the church of Santa Maria del Carmine in Florence. It depicts the expulsion of Adam and Eve from the garden of Eden, from the biblical Book of Genesis chapter 3, albeit with a few differences from the canonical account.",
      "facts": [
        "These were later removed in the 1980s when the painting was fully restored and cleaned.",
        "Many possible sources of inspiration have been pointed out that Masaccio may have drawn from."
