      "imageWidth": 3925,
      "imageHeight": 3925,
      "story": "This painting, also commonly known as The Berlin Tondo, is a desco da parto, or birth tray, painted by the Italian Renaissance artist Masaccio. Stylistic analysis shows similarities with his San Giovenale Triptych, an early work of the painter from 1422, and the birth tray is dated a short time after it at around 1423. With the frame around it, the tondo has a diameter of 66 cm.",
      "facts": [
        "The upper side of the tray shows a scene soon (probably a few days) after the actual birth of a child.",
